    <!-- ==================================================================
         Application Information (narrative sections remain supported)
         ================================================================== -->
    <ApplicationNotes>
        <Section title="Overview">
            <Paragraph>
                The LM5116 device is a step-down DC-DC controller used to convert a
                higher DC voltage to a lower DC voltage. Use the design procedure in
                this section to select external component values, or use the WEBENCH
                Power Designer software to generate a complete design.
            </Paragraph>
        </Section>
        <Section title="Typical Application: 5-V, 7-A Design Example">
            <Parameter>
                <Name>Output voltage</Name>
                <Typical unit="V">5</Typical>
            </Parameter>
            <Parameter>
                <Name>Input voltage range</Name>
                <Minimum unit="V">7</Minimum>
                <Maximum unit="V">60</Maximum>
            </Parameter>
            <Parameter>
                <Name>Maximum load current</Name>
                <Typical unit="A">7</Typical>
            </Parameter>
            <Parameter>
                <Name>Switching frequency</Name>
                <Typical unit="kHz">250</Typical>
            </Parameter>
            <Paragraph>
                RT is calculated from RT = (T - 450 ns) / 284 pF, where T = 1 / fSW.
                For 250 kHz this gives 12.5 kOhm; the nearest standard value of
                12.4 kOhm was chosen.
            </Paragraph>
        </Section>
        <Section title="Layout Guidelines">
            <Paragraph>
                In a buck regulator, the primary switching loop consists of the input
                capacitor, MOSFETs, and current sense resistor. Minimizing the area of
                this loop reduces stray inductance and minimizes noise. The input
                capacitor must be placed as close as possible to the MOSFETs, with the
                VIN side connected directly to the high-side MOSFET drain. Connect the
                AGND and PGND pins together through a topside copper area covering the
                entire underside of the device, with several vias to the ground plane.
            </Paragraph>
        </Section>
    </ApplicationNotes>

